038 #edb/ref 17592186342102 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068687 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186385993 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068687 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186392568 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068687 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186507497 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068687 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186507522 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068687 #edb/ref 1039 "Representing Solutions of Compound Inequalities on Number Lines" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068687 #edb/ref 1041 #edb/ref 17592186068474 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068687 #edb/ref 1042 #uuid "b3ff37f0-6e45-5da4-ac87-1b93c8df3e80" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068935 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186069552 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068935 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186069553 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068935 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186069554 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068935 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186069555 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068935 #edb/ref 1044 #edb/ref 17592186045463 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068935 #edb/ref 1045 "Solving Compound Inequalities" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068935 #edb/ref 1046 #edb/ref 17592186069552 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068935 #edb/ref 1049 #edb/ref 17592186050734 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068935 #edb/ref 1050 480.0 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068935 #edb/ref 1050 480.0 #edb/ref 17592186045436] [17592186068935 #edb/ref 1053 #uuid "a71fc11d-26f8-54c9-8cba-9f88ebf49ad8" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186069226 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186066534 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186069226 #edb/ref 1069 "q-3063" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186069226 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186069226 #edb/ref 1071 "Solve the inequality $-9<-3x+8<-5.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186069226 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "793dd364-450f-5a57-9269-620a4ed6531f" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186069226 #edb/ref 1074 "We isolate $x$ by applying the addition and multiplication principles, as usual. \n\nFirst, we apply the addition principle:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-9 & <-3x+8<-5 \\\\ -9-8 & <-3x+8-8<-5-8 \\\\ -17 & <-3x<-13\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we divide by $-3.$ Note that since we are dividing by a negative number, we need to flip the inequality signs.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-17 & <-3x<-13 \\\\ \\frac{-17}{-3} & >\\frac{-3x}{-3}>\\frac{-13}{-3} \\\\ \\frac{17}{3} & >x>\\frac{13}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nThe solution can be written as $\\frac{17}{3}>x>\\frac{13}{3}$, but this is somewhat difficult to read because the larger number is on the left rather than the right. So, we will rewrite the solution by reversing the order of the numbers: \n\n$$\n\\frac{13}{3}<x<\\frac{17}{3}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186069351 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186067276 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186069351 #edb/ref 1069 "q-44745" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186069351 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186069351 #edb/ref 1071 "Which of the following number lines gives the solution to $-3\\le 2x-1\\le 5?$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186069351 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "a50fbeb7-374f-57aa-97cb-71f55ec85260" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186069351 #edb/ref 1074 "We isolate $x$  by applying the addition and multiplication principles, as usual.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-3 & \\le 2x-1\\le 5 \\\\ -3+1 & \\le 2x-1+1\\le 5+1 \\\\ -2 & \\le 2x\\le 6 \\\\ \\frac{-2}{2} & \\le \\frac{2x}{2}\\le \\frac{6}{2} \\\\ -1 & \\le x\\le 3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can represent this solution using a number line, as follows. \n\n![](images/76/76b6a19b3104f122989479a681709af3ca0bf8c05c59f76dc2c7707643980398.png)" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186069352 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186067282 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186069352 #edb/ref 1069 "q-44758" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186069352 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186069352 #edb/ref 1071 "Which of the following number lines gives the solution to $-5\\le -2x+3\\le 5?$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186069352 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "bc79035c-5b95-5816-b7f8-1b0d00701572" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186069352 #edb/ref 1074 "We isolate $x$ by applying the addition and multiplication principles, as usual. \n\nFirst, we apply the addition principle:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-5 & \\le -2x+3\\le 5 \\\\ -5-3 & \\le -2x+3-3\\le 5-3 \\\\ -8 & \\le -2x\\le 2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we divide by $-2.$ Note that since we are dividing by a negative number, we need to flip the inequality signs. \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-8 & \\le -2x\\le 2 \\\\ \\frac{-8}{-2} & \\ge \\frac{-2x}{-2}\\ge \\frac{2}{-2} \\\\ \\frac{8}{2} & \\ge x\\ge -\\frac{2}{2} \\\\ 4 & \\ge x\\ge -1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe solution can be written as $4\\ge x\\ge -1$, but this is somewhat difficult to read because the larger number is on the left rather than the right. So, we will rewrite the solution by reversing the order of the numbers: \n\n$$\n-1\\le x\\le 4\n$$\n\nWe can represent this solution using a number line, as follows.\n\n![](images/c4/c4f4ab05b534287dc75765b83dc23cbdfe42044aeddea220510668fbc6b8b51c.png)" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186069552 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186069553 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186069552 #edb/ref 1061 108821 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186069552 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "83b17106-05a3-58df-89b9-4510e4dbee9f" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186069552 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186070018 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186069553 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186069554 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186069553 #edb/ref 1061 108822 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186069553 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "7ff1eeef-0d3b-5cde-9aca-5461fbfa7dee" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186069553 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186068685 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186069554 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186069555 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186069554 #edb/ref 1061 108825 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186069554 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "60d28d8b-03d2-535c-826f-3510ebac457f" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186069554 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186068686 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186069555 #edb/ref 1061 108828 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186069555 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "5885620e-83f2-528b-862e-d400efe5fd7c" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186069555 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186068687 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186070018 #edb/ref 1064 "Suppose that we wish to solve the compound inequality \n\n$$\n4 \\le x + 2 \\le 8.\n$$\n\nTo solve the compound inequality, we apply the usual operations to the middle of the inequality to isolate $x.$ Keep in mind that whatever we do to the middle, we also need to do to *both* the left-hand *and* right-hand sides.\n\nHere, we can isolate $x$ by subtracting $2\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\eqalign{\n\t4 & \\le x + 2 \\le 8 \\[5pt]\n\t4 \\,{\\color{red}-}\\, {\\color{red}{2}} &\\le x + 2 \\,{\\color{red}-}\\, {\\color{red}{2}} \\le 8 \\,{\\color{red}-}\\, {\\color{red}{2}} \\[5pt]\n\t2 &\\le x \\le 6\n}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $2 \\le x \\le 6.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186070018 #edb/ref 1065 8677 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186070018 #edb/ref 1066 #uuid "6d8fae47-5e67-5793-a585-d3781d5c4555" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186070018 #edb/ref 1067 "Introduction" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186541419 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186542235 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186541419 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186542268 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186541419 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186542276 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186541419 #edb/ref 1044 #edb/ref 17592186045464 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186541419 #edb/ref 1045 "Solving Compound Inequalities" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186541419 #edb/ref 1046 #edb/ref 17592186542268 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186541419 #edb/ref 1048 #edb/ref 17592186046647 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186541419 #edb/ref 1049 #edb/ref 17592186050734 #edb/ref 17592186045